712
00:51:23.413 --> 00:51:25.206
Cut his head off!

713
00:51:25.290 --> 00:51:29.085
Listen, everybody!
This don't change nothin'!

714
00:51:29.169 --> 00:51:32.379
We played as a team, we won as a team.

715
00:51:32.464 --> 00:51:34.590
Just because the waterboy's a cheater

716
00:51:34.674 --> 00:51:37.510
don't change the fact
that the real Mud Dogs

717
00:51:37.594 --> 00:51:40.096
are gonna kick some Cougar ass.

718
00:51:40.180 --> 00:51:42.431
Mud Dogs! Mud Dogs!

719
00:51:42.516 --> 00:51:47.061
Mud Dogs! Mud Dogs!
Mud Dogs! Mud Dogs!

720
00:51:55.320 --> 00:51:57.279
Let's do it!

721
00:52:04.037 --> 00:52:05.579
Sorry, Bobby.

722
00:52:14.005 --> 00:52:17.007
Believe me, I understand.

723
00:52:17.092 --> 00:52:19.677
Yeah, and you're
deeply appreciated, Mr. Dodd.

724
00:52:19.761 --> 00:52:22.721
Thank you so much. Bye-bye.

725
00:52:24.307 --> 00:52:27.810
Good news. The NCAA is gonna
allow you to play in the Bourbon Bowl.

726
00:52:27.894 --> 00:52:29.645
- Yes.
- You have to pass

727
00:52:29.729 --> 00:52:34.692
- the high school equivalency test.
- It's not the test, coach.

728
00:52:34.776 --> 00:52:37.945
Everybody... hates me.

729
00:52:39.823 --> 00:52:41.657
That's not true.

730
00:52:41.741 --> 00:52:44.910
One man said he wanted
to decapitate me.

731
00:52:44.995 --> 00:52:48.831
Nobody else thought that
to be too bad of an idea.

732
00:52:51.835 --> 00:52:54.003
Somebody made me look like a cheater.

733
00:52:54.087 --> 00:52:57.673
I did it. I did it.
I did it! I did it! I did it!

734
00:52:57.757 --> 00:53:01.635
- It was me.
- Why?

735
00:53:05.390 --> 00:53:10.269
Because I wanted you to play.
Because you were my way out, Bobby.

736
00:53:10.353 --> 00:53:13.522
It was the only way to get you in.

737
00:53:13.607 --> 00:53:15.274
I am so sorry.

738
00:53:16.193 --> 00:53:19.028
Why didn't you stick up for me
down by the river?

739
00:53:22.240 --> 00:53:26.118
The truth is... I fled.

740
00:53:26.203 --> 00:53:28.954
I came into my office,
I went under my desk, I cried.

741
00:53:29.039 --> 00:53:31.957
I cried.
I cried like a ten-year-old girl!

742
00:53:39.466 --> 00:53:41.091
Red and I have a history.

743
00:53:41.176 --> 00:53:44.178
Twenty years ago,
we were assistants to Coach Cavanaugh

744
00:53:44.262 --> 00:53:48.515
at the University of Louisiana.
Red ran the practices

745
00:53:48.600 --> 00:53:51.769
and I used to come up with the plays.

746
00:53:51.853 --> 00:53:55.147
Oh, boy, was I good.

747
00:53:56.233 --> 00:54:01.153
I  would  write these foolproof plays
in my little green notebook that I had.

748
00:54:01.238 --> 00:54:03.906
The opposition
didn't even know what hit 'em.

749
00:54:03.990 --> 00:54:07.034
And  when Coach Cavanaugh
was going to retire, me and Red,

750
00:54:07.118 --> 00:54:09.954
we knew that one of us
was gonna be his successor.

751
00:54:13.375 --> 00:54:15.668
- Hey, Red.
- How ya doin'?

752
00:54:17.545 --> 00:54:21.090
- Come by to wish me luck?
- Well, not exactly, no, no.

753
00:54:21.174 --> 00:54:25.344
Actually, I come by to get you
to do ol' Red a little favor.

754
00:54:25.428 --> 00:54:29.265
- Sure. What's up?
- Well, you know that green notebook

755
00:54:29.349 --> 00:54:31.684
you use to write all them
football plays in?

756
00:54:31.768 --> 00:54:36.021
Well, I need to show Cavanaugh that
I can come up with some good play ideas.

757
00:54:36.106 --> 00:54:38.190
But you didn't come up with them.

758
00:54:39.109 --> 00:54:42.444
They're my plays. I need them.

759
00:54:42.529 --> 00:54:48.117
Klein, I'm gonna have this book,
one way or another.

760
00:54:48.201 --> 00:54:51.078
You might as well let the thing
go, 'cause if you don't,

761
00:54:51.162 --> 00:54:53.956
it's gonna get awfully,
awfully physical here.

762
00:54:54.040 --> 00:54:56.542
And I don't think
you want that, do you?

763
00:55:02.048 --> 00:55:05.801
Of course, Red got the job.
Next day, fired me.

764
00:55:05.885 --> 00:55:08.137
Once he had my notebook,
he didn't need me.

765
00:55:11.099 --> 00:55:12.558
I didn't take it very well.

766
00:55:12.642 --> 00:55:16.061
No, Grandma, I didn't get it.

767
00:55:16.146 --> 00:55:18.605
I can't believe it myself.

768
00:55:18.690 --> 00:55:22.568
I know. I'm so numb.

769
00:55:23.903 --> 00:55:26.196
I just hate him,
I hate him, I hate him.

770
00:55:28.074 --> 00:55:30.409
That is a terrible story, coach.

771
00:55:30.493 --> 00:55:33.120
But why don't you just come up
with some new plays?

772
00:55:33.204 --> 00:55:35.581
- I tried. I can't.
- Yes.

773
00:55:35.665 --> 00:55:38.334
I guess I have a mental block
ever since

774
00:55:38.418 --> 00:55:41.170
Red took my playbook
and my manhood.

775
00:55:41.254 --> 00:55:44.381
I knew what he was gonna do!

776
00:55:45.216 --> 00:55:47.843
And I just didn't fight back.

777
00:55:47.927 --> 00:55:51.764
Well, you're gonna show him
that you're a man on Saturday.

778
00:55:53.600 --> 00:55:58.187
I'm gonna show everybody that
I'm not a dummy. I'm gonna go study.

779
00:56:03.818 --> 00:56:08.447
Mama, maybe you could stop
brushin' my hair so I can read.

780
00:56:08.531 --> 00:56:12.701
Read? You don't have to read.

781
00:56:15.538 --> 00:56:19.333
- What you readin' for?
- 'Cause I enjoys it, Mama.

782
00:56:19.417 --> 00:56:23.003
Don't look like to me you enjoys it,
sittin' there all grouchy.

783
00:56:23.088 --> 00:56:26.507
Mama, I gotta read this book
and six other books tonight,

784
00:56:26.591 --> 00:56:28.717
or else I can't play foot...

785
00:56:32.972 --> 00:56:34.807
- ...ball.
- Foosball?

786
00:56:34.891 --> 00:56:37.893
You playin' the foosball behind my back?

787
00:56:37.977 --> 00:56:40.562
The reason I'm doin' this
so I can go to school.

788
00:56:40.647 --> 00:56:44.024
School?! You goin' to school?!

789
00:56:45.276 --> 00:56:47.736
Sorry, Mama. I wanted to tell you.

790
00:56:47.821 --> 00:56:52.157
You off gallivantin' with your fancy
foosball friends at school,

791
00:56:52.242 --> 00:56:56.245
while I'm sittin' here all day
with nobody to keep me company

792
00:56:56.329 --> 00:56:59.248
except Steve?

793
00:56:59.332 --> 00:57:01.583
The chickens
are comin' home to roost.

794
00:57:01.668 --> 00:57:04.670
You reap the fruit
of your selfish ways.

795
00:57:04.754 --> 00:57:07.589
You're gonna lose all your
fancy foosball games

796
00:57:07.674 --> 00:57:10.926
and you're gonna fail your big exam,
because school is...

797
00:57:11.010 --> 00:57:12.928
The devil?

798
00:57:13.012 --> 00:57:16.223
Everything is the devil to you, Mama!

799
00:57:16.307 --> 00:57:19.935
Well, I like school
and I like football!

800
00:57:20.019 --> 00:57:23.856
And I'm gonna keep doin' them both
because they make me feel good!

801
00:57:25.316 --> 00:57:28.235
And by the way, Mama,
alligators are ornery

802
00:57:28.319 --> 00:57:30.404
because of their medulla oblongata!

803
00:57:36.369 --> 00:57:39.413
And I like Vicki,
and she likes me back!

804
00:57:39.497 --> 00:57:42.249
And she showed me her boobies,
and I liked them too!

805
00:57:56.764 --> 00:58:00.184
The Louisiana High School
Equivalency Examination

806
00:58:00.268 --> 00:58:03.896
consists of 300
multiple choice questions.

807
00:58:03.980 --> 00:58:07.191
You have three hours.
Good luck to you, sir.

808
00:58:39.265 --> 00:58:42.142
Ben Franklin.

809
00:58:43.770 --> 00:58:46.772
Mama, when did Ben Franklin
invent electricity?

810
00:58:46.856 --> 00:58:49.775
That's nonsense!
I invented electricity.

811
00:58:50.610 --> 00:58:52.945
Ben Franklin is the devil!

812
00:59:03.623 --> 00:59:06.500
I can't believe you got a 97!

813
00:59:06.584 --> 00:59:10.629
I can't believe I told Mama
that I got feelings for you.

814
00:59:10.713 --> 00:59:14.967
Well, welcome to your manhood,
Bobby Boucher.

815
00:59:15.051 --> 00:59:18.095
When we get a little more time,
I'll welcome you properly.

816
00:59:18.179 --> 00:59:21.306
Yes, once again, I'm not quite sure
what that means, but...

817
00:59:21.391 --> 00:59:24.560
We should get goin'. I told Coach
I'd drive to the game with him.

818
00:59:28.439 --> 00:59:32.150
I was with you from two to four
last night. You tell them.

819
00:59:33.820 --> 00:59:38.240
Bobby, your mama got sick this mornin'.
She's in the hospital.

820
00:59:40.493 --> 00:59:43.203
Mama, what have I done?

821
00:59:43.288 --> 00:59:44.997
I'm so sorry, Mama.

822
00:59:48.334 --> 00:59:52.087
Doctors say they can't figure out
what's wrong with her.

823
00:59:53.339 --> 00:59:55.340
But I know what's wrong.

824
00:59:55.425 --> 00:59:57.593
She got a broken heart
because of me.

825
00:59:57.677 --> 00:59:59.761
Bobby, that's ridiculous.

826
00:59:59.846 --> 01:00:03.890
Everybody else in this town
turn on me at the drop of a hat.

827
01:00:04.976 --> 01:00:09.271
Mama is the only one who really cares
if I live or die.

828
01:00:09.355 --> 01:00:13.567
She my whole world.
Will you just leave us alone?

829
01:00:15.028 --> 01:00:17.904
She'll be fine, Bobby.
We better get going.

830
01:00:17.989 --> 01:00:21.116
God knows what the team is doing
with Farmer Fran watching.

831
01:00:44.724 --> 01:00:47.059
You really made it look like home.

832
01:00:55.234 --> 01:00:56.276
How's that, Steve?

833
01:01:14.921 --> 01:01:18.507
Take a look. The crowd has
never been bigger. Know  why?

834
01:01:18.591 --> 01:01:23.136
Look who's on the television, Mama.
The devil.

835
01:01:23.221 --> 01:01:25.806
...500,000 intimate friends...

836
01:01:36.651 --> 01:01:38.610
Who that? Who there?

837
01:01:51.290 --> 01:01:54.543
Three, two, one!

838
01:01:54.627 --> 01:01:57.754
- Happy New Year!
- Happy New Year, Mama.

839
01:01:59.590 --> 01:02:03.802
My resolution is to
never hurt you again.

840
01:02:09.142 --> 01:02:17.983
Waterboy! Waterboy!

841
01:02:47.346 --> 01:02:51.391
Bobby Boucher, all these folks
are here tonight

842
01:02:51.476 --> 01:02:53.560
to tell you that they're sorry,

843
01:02:53.644 --> 01:02:58.440
that they're sorry for not supportin'
you when it meant the most.

844
01:02:58.524 --> 01:03:03.945
But you do have friends, and one of 'em
wants to say somethin'. Come on.

845
01:03:08.159 --> 01:03:12.287
I am not what you would call
a handsome man.

846
01:03:12.371 --> 01:03:15.123
The good Lord chose not
to bless me

847
01:03:15.208 --> 01:03:19.461
with charm, athletic ability

848
01:03:19.545 --> 01:03:21.922
or a fully functional brain.

849
01:03:23.341 --> 01:03:27.427
You see, you're an inspiration

850
01:03:27.512 --> 01:03:31.139
to all of us
who weren't born handsome

851
01:03:31.224 --> 01:03:36.978
and charming and cool and...

852
01:03:39.774 --> 01:03:44.820
- I can't! I can't!
- It's OK.

853
01:03:44.904 --> 01:03:49.574
Bobby, if your mama could only hear us
right now, we would tell her

854
01:03:49.659 --> 01:03:52.661
what a fine boy she raised,

855
01:03:52.745 --> 01:03:56.832
and how much your playing football
means to this town.

856
01:03:56.916 --> 01:04:01.461
But she can't hear you
'cause she's unconscious.

857
01:04:03.172 --> 01:04:08.760
I'm sorry to disappoint you all,
but please keep your voices down

858
01:04:08.845 --> 01:04:11.596
so my mama can get her rest.

859
01:04:20.147 --> 01:04:23.441
Well, wake her ass up!
We gotta win tomorrow!

860
01:04:45.631 --> 01:04:50.135
Mama! Thank God you're OK.
I'm so sorry.

861
01:04:50.219 --> 01:04:52.679
I was so bad.
You were right about everything.

862
01:04:52.763 --> 01:04:55.015
- I've been a knucklehead.
- Hush, baby.

863
01:04:55.099 --> 01:04:59.603
You should've seen this
a long time ago.

864
01:04:59.687 --> 01:05:03.231
- Oh, my word! Is that my daddy?
- No, no.

865
01:05:03.316 --> 01:05:06.484
That's a guy I dated
before I met your father.

866
01:05:06.569 --> 01:05:09.321
You could iron a shirt
on his stomach.

867
01:05:09.405 --> 01:05:13.074
Well, that was lust, not love.
Turn the page.

868
01:05:16.412 --> 01:05:18.496
There's your daddy.

869
01:05:18.581 --> 01:05:20.707
So handsome.

870
01:05:21.792 --> 01:05:23.043
Read on.

871
01:05:25.004 --> 01:05:27.714
"Dear Helen." Who's Helen?

872
01:05:29.675 --> 01:05:31.760
That's my first name, Bobby.

873
01:05:36.140 --> 01:05:38.433
"I have arrived here in New Orleans.

874
01:05:38.517 --> 01:05:41.603
It is even more beautiful
than in the picture book.

875
01:05:41.687 --> 01:05:44.439
I'm sure I'll have
no problem finding work,

876
01:05:44.523 --> 01:05:48.610
so you can expect my next letter
to contain lots of money.

877
01:05:48.694 --> 01:05:52.781
Your loving husband, Robert."
That's nice, Mama.

878
01:05:53.950 --> 01:05:57.202
"Dear Helen." That's you.

879
01:05:57.286 --> 01:06:00.538
"I found a job as a lemonade vendor,

880
01:06:00.623 --> 01:06:02.666
but sorry, no money yet.

881
01:06:02.750 --> 01:06:05.418
New Orleans is an expensive city.

882
01:06:05.503 --> 01:06:10.590
Expensive, but fun.
Hope all is well. Robert."

883
01:06:12.009 --> 01:06:14.469
"To Whom It May Concern:

884
01:06:14.553 --> 01:06:17.263
This will be my last letter.

885
01:06:17.348 --> 01:06:20.809
We have grown apart
over these last six weeks.

886
01:06:20.893 --> 01:06:25.105
I now have two loves in my life:

887
01:06:25.189 --> 01:06:29.651
Big-city livin'
and a voodoo woman named Phyllis.

888
01:06:29.735 --> 01:06:32.737
Ciao, Roberto."

889
01:06:32.822 --> 01:06:36.324
He changed his name to Roberto.

890
01:06:36.409 --> 01:06:38.827
I guess he thought it was more exotic.

891
01:06:38.911 --> 01:06:41.830
But Mama says that...
I mean, you say that...

892
01:06:41.914 --> 01:06:46.584
Bobby, your daddy
didn't go into no Peace Corps.

893
01:06:47.920 --> 01:06:50.005
He deserted us, baby.

894
01:06:52.258 --> 01:06:56.636
No, no, Mama. You shouldn't be dredgin'
up painful memories in your condition.

895
01:06:56.721 --> 01:06:59.347
Hush. Your mama's
as healthy as an ox,

896
01:06:59.432 --> 01:07:01.766
and as dumb as one to boot.

897
01:07:01.851 --> 01:07:04.602
I was so scared you'd abandon me too.

898
01:07:04.687 --> 01:07:09.941
And I made you abandon
all those people who depend on ya.

899
01:07:10.026 --> 01:07:12.861
I hid you away from the world,
Bobby Boucher.

900
01:07:12.945 --> 01:07:16.531
But I can't hog you
to myself no more,

901
01:07:16.615 --> 01:07:19.701
because everyone's seen
how wonderful you are.

902
01:07:21.078 --> 01:07:22.620
Oh, Mama!

903
01:07:24.248 --> 01:07:25.790
Now...

904
01:07:28.002 --> 01:07:31.212
You go play foosball
with your friends.

905
01:07:31.297 --> 01:07:34.299
Welcome to ABC's coverage
of the Bourbon Bowl.

906
01:07:34.383 --> 01:07:37.844
Good afternoon. I'm Brent Musburger
with my colleague Dan Fouts.

907
01:07:37.928 --> 01:07:41.389
The big story here is a game
that's lost some of its luster

908
01:07:41.474 --> 01:07:45.393
without its star player,
the waterboy, Bobby Boucher.

909
01:07:45.478 --> 01:07:48.313
Red's got a couple
of solid early rounders out there.

910
01:07:48.397 --> 01:07:52.484
I know, but I really wanted to scout
that waterboy. Reminds me of Greg Lloyd.

911
01:07:52.568 --> 01:07:54.527
- Zack Thomas.
- Whatever.

912
01:07:54.612 --> 01:07:56.362
Is she ready?

913
01:07:56.447 --> 01:07:59.240
Oh, yeah. She's more than ready.

914
01:07:59.325 --> 01:08:02.035
Come on, Bobby!
You'll miss the boat!

915
01:08:08.084 --> 01:08:09.250
Let's go, ladies.

916
01:08:14.840 --> 01:08:19.511
We are underway!
The opening kickoff is a beauty!

917
01:08:22.306 --> 01:08:25.225
Holdsworth is gonna bring it out
from nine yards deep.

918
01:08:25.309 --> 01:08:26.935
Come on.

919
01:08:27.019 --> 01:08:28.353
Yeah!

920
01:08:29.355 --> 01:08:33.108
They're showing no respect
for this team without Boucher.

921
01:08:33.192 --> 01:08:37.278
Good reason, Brent.
109 yards untouched.

922
01:08:37.863 --> 01:08:40.532
Touchdown, Cougars! They strike first.

923
01:08:47.706 --> 01:08:51.459
Time running down in the first quarter.
Cougars lead is 17-nothing.

924
01:08:53.671 --> 01:08:55.755
Set!

925
01:08:55.840 --> 01:08:57.382
Three, 33!

926
01:08:58.717 --> 01:09:01.761
Three, 33! Hut!

927
01:09:02.763 --> 01:09:05.765
That quarterback can't
get the ball off before he's hit.

928
01:09:05.850 --> 01:09:09.102
It's as if they're in
the offensive huddle with him.

929
01:09:12.898 --> 01:09:15.567
Are you gonna finish
that hot dog, Jimmy?

930
01:09:15.651 --> 01:09:16.818
Now I'm not.

931
01:09:16.902 --> 01:09:19.946
Mama, you think
we'll make it on time?

932
01:09:20.030 --> 01:09:23.908
Hang on! I'll show you what
A.J. Foyt taught me.

933
01:09:27.913 --> 01:09:30.665
The end of the half.
The Cougars are dominating.

934
01:09:30.749 --> 01:09:34.294
Let's hope the Mud Dogs
can make some adjustments.

935
01:09:34.378 --> 01:09:36.671
Well, they better, because they suck.

936
01:09:42.428 --> 01:09:44.470
Anybody got an idea?

937
01:09:48.934 --> 01:09:50.268
Hey.

938
01:09:52.605 --> 01:09:55.857
Remember the time Bobby tackled
the referee by mistake?

939
01:09:56.942 --> 01:09:59.110
Yeah, that was pretty funny.

940
01:09:59.195 --> 01:10:02.030
How about the time he tackled
the guy from Louisville

941
01:10:02.114 --> 01:10:04.199
and threw him into the stands?

942
01:10:06.452 --> 01:10:11.372
Y'all remember when he intercepted
the ball and his pants fell off?

943
01:10:11.457 --> 01:10:14.375
And then he ran
for the touchdown bare-assed.

944
01:10:26.055 --> 01:10:28.723
Remember when Bobby Boucher
showed up at halftime

945
01:10:28.807 --> 01:10:30.683
and Mud Dogs won the Bourbon Bowl?

946
01:10:31.555 --> 01:10:35.555
[Encode, Sync or Sub by AreLift]

947
01:10:37.816 --> 01:10:41.736
Hey, sorry about givin' you
so much shit this year.

948
01:10:41.820 --> 01:10:44.239
You're the heart and soul
of this team, Bobby.

949
01:10:44.323 --> 01:10:47.033
The only one of us
who could've passed that test.

950
01:10:47.117 --> 01:10:51.246
Thank you all so much
for being my friends.

951
01:10:51.330 --> 01:10:55.416
Let's wait till later to hold hands
and kiss. We got a bowl game to win.

952
01:10:55.501 --> 01:10:57.752
- Yeah!
- Two, three!

953
01:10:57.836 --> 01:10:58.795
Mud Dogs!

954
01:10:58.879 --> 01:11:04.801
In a dramatic turn of events,
Bobby Boucherjust arrived at halftime.

955
01:11:04.885 --> 01:11:09.430
And on a fan boat, Brent. His mother
drove him right into the stadium.

956
01:11:18.440 --> 01:11:21.359
Waterboy! Waterboy!

957
01:11:27.783 --> 01:11:30.660
Foosball's not for the devil.

958
01:11:30.744 --> 01:11:32.453
It's for my Bobby.

959
01:11:32.538 --> 01:11:35.665
Time to open up some whoop-ass.

960
01:11:42.798 --> 01:11:46.592
Shit, he showed up.
All right, look.

961
01:11:46.677 --> 01:11:48.428
Just relax. Relax.

962
01:11:48.512 --> 01:11:51.306
Go in there and do exactly
like we planned. Go, go, go!

963
01:11:51.390 --> 01:11:53.725
This could be the start
of some high drama.

964
01:11:53.809 --> 01:11:58.980
Or are the Mud Dogs too far behind?
Bobby Boucher is on defense.

965
01:11:59.064 --> 01:12:02.650
The Cougars are coming out
from their own 20-yard line.

966
01:12:02.735 --> 01:12:05.194
The pitch. It's a reverse!

967
01:12:05.279 --> 01:12:07.822
Boucher's not fooled.

968
01:12:07.906 --> 01:12:10.241
Fumble! Robideaux's got it!

969
01:12:10.326 --> 01:12:12.410
Touchdown, Mud Dogs!

970
01:12:14.705 --> 01:12:18.416
- Boucher knocked the poop out of him.
- "Poop"?

971
01:12:18.500 --> 01:12:23.671
Slap hands! Slap hands!

972
01:12:25.424 --> 01:12:29.677
Drink up, now. I want you girls
to sober up. Have faith in my Bobby.

973
01:12:29.762 --> 01:12:33.306
The Mud Dogs are faced
with yet another third and long.

974
01:12:33.390 --> 01:12:35.808
- Hut!
- Grenouille back to pass.

975
01:12:35.893 --> 01:12:38.561
He's gonna be stuffed again!
The Mud Dogs offense

976
01:12:38.645 --> 01:12:42.398
is still unable to move that ball.
But the way their defense is fired up,

977
01:12:42.483 --> 01:12:45.193
they still have a shot
at winning this game.

978
01:12:45.277 --> 01:12:47.737
Look. Now what ifwe...

979
01:12:51.617 --> 01:12:54.118
Trust me. Go, go, go, go, go.

980
01:12:55.412 --> 01:12:59.874
The Cougars lead 27-7
in the middle of the third quarter.

981
01:12:59.958 --> 01:13:01.793
And he takes a knee?

982
01:13:01.877 --> 01:13:04.462
Y'all gonna play or what?

983
01:13:07.049 --> 01:13:09.050
How do you all like my new offense?

984
01:13:11.804 --> 01:13:16.015
All right, it's second and 12,
as the Cougars line up on the ball.

985
01:13:19.895 --> 01:13:23.147
What is Red Beaulieu doing,
refusing to play offense?

986
01:13:23.232 --> 01:13:26.025
- Dan, this is bizarre.
- No, it's not, Brent.

987
01:13:26.110 --> 01:13:29.404
It's brilliant. Red is
taking the Waterboy out of the game.

988
01:13:29.488 --> 01:13:32.073
By kneeling down
three times and punting,

989
01:13:32.157 --> 01:13:34.200
he'll make the Mud Dog
offense try to beat him.

990
01:13:34.284 --> 01:13:36.702
The way they're playing,
that's impossible.

991
01:13:36.787 --> 01:13:38.871
The Mud Dog's most valuable player,

992
01:13:38.956 --> 01:13:42.083
the linebacker they call "The Waterboy,"
is now powerless.

993
01:13:42.167 --> 01:13:46.963
That means Coach Klein will have
to find another way to outfox Red.

994
01:13:49.133 --> 01:13:51.342
Mud Dogs call a timeout.

995
01:13:53.011 --> 01:13:56.055
Mr. Coach Klein. Mr. Coach Klein!
Mr. Coach Klein!

996
01:13:57.516 --> 01:14:01.769
- Where are you going?
- I was just gonna get a hot pretzel.

997
01:14:01.854 --> 01:14:04.772
Mr. Coach Klein,
are you afraid of Red Beaulieu?

998
01:14:09.027 --> 01:14:10.445
I am petrified of him.

999
01:14:10.529 --> 01:14:13.614
Well, why don't you pretend
that Red Beaulieu

1000
01:14:13.699 --> 01:14:15.908
is somebody that you're not afraid of.

1001
01:14:15.993 --> 01:14:18.453
- Pretend?
- Yes.

1002
01:14:18.537 --> 01:14:20.955
Visualize somebody you're not afraid of.

1003
01:14:21.039 --> 01:14:24.625
- And then attack, like you told me.
- I'll try.

1004
01:14:24.710 --> 01:14:26.169
He's right over there.

1005
01:14:39.766 --> 01:14:42.894
Little baby. Yeah.

1006
01:14:43.896 --> 01:14:46.314
Hello, little baby.

1007
01:14:51.862 --> 01:14:54.322
A poo-poo?
Do you have a poo-poo?

1008
01:14:54.406 --> 01:14:58.826
Yes. OK. Now.

1009
01:14:58.911 --> 01:15:01.787
This is what we're gonna do.
He's gonna come here...

1010
01:15:10.255 --> 01:15:12.590
Come and get this one, Cougars.

1011
01:15:12.674 --> 01:15:15.426
Red 22! Hike!

1012
01:15:15.511 --> 01:15:18.179
Snap to Grenouille. A reverse!

1013
01:15:18.263 --> 01:15:22.016
No, it's a double reverse!
Oh, what a block!

1014
01:15:22.100 --> 01:15:26.187
And Bugge springs free!
Trouble! Lateral!

1015
01:15:26.271 --> 01:15:28.856
Got him! What a play!

1016
01:15:28.941 --> 01:15:32.068
Grenouille to the 15, the ten,
the five!

1017
01:15:32.152 --> 01:15:35.196
- Touchdown, Mud Dogs!
- Well, well, well.

1018
01:15:35.280 --> 01:15:37.949
Coach Klein does have
a few tricks up his sleeve.

1019
01:15:38.033 --> 01:15:41.327
What the hell...
What the hell is this?

1020
01:15:41.411 --> 01:15:45.039
We go from a championship
football team to a bunch of dogs!

1021
01:15:45.123 --> 01:15:48.626
Right now, we're going to go
to the sidelines and Lynn Swann.

1022
01:15:48.710 --> 01:15:51.796
- What do you have for us?
- I'm with Vicki Vallencourt,

1023
01:15:51.880 --> 01:15:54.966
taking over Bobby Boucher's
water duties for this game.

1024
01:15:55.050 --> 01:15:58.970
I'm not takin' over.
I'm just tryin' not to screw up too bad.

1025
01:15:59.054 --> 01:16:02.390
Let me ask you. What's your prediction
for the rest of this game?

1026
01:16:02.474 --> 01:16:05.935
- Mud Dogs are gonna win, 30-27.
- That's very interesting.

1027
01:16:06.019 --> 01:16:09.730
- How'd you come up with that guess?
- Guess? That ain't no guess!

1028
01:16:09.815 --> 01:16:12.400
- That's what it's gonna be.
- OK. That's fine.

1029
01:16:12.484 --> 01:16:14.110
Be careful down there.

1030
01:16:18.240 --> 01:16:19.991
All right. Where's Meaney?

1031
01:16:20.075 --> 01:16:22.118
- Meaney?
- Here, coach.

1032
01:16:22.202 --> 01:16:24.787
Get in there and see
if that waterboy can stop you.

1033
01:16:24.871 --> 01:16:25.871
- Yes, sir!
- Go!

1034
01:16:25.956 --> 01:16:31.460
Red is sending his best defender in as a
running back? What do you make of this?

1035
01:16:31.545 --> 01:16:34.463
He's gotta find some way
to neutralize the Waterboy.

1036
01:16:34.548 --> 01:16:37.091
He probably thinks Meaney
will pound it in there

1037
01:16:37.175 --> 01:16:40.052
- like Fridge did for the Bears.
- Hey, Waterboy!

1038
01:16:40.137 --> 01:16:42.430
Is your girlfriend
gonna save you again?

1039
01:16:42.514 --> 01:16:45.266
No. I'll take matters
into my own hands. You'll see.

1040
01:16:45.350 --> 01:16:47.435
Bring it to the hole!
Your ass is mine!

1041
01:16:51.898 --> 01:16:54.108
You sound like a big choo-choo train.

1042
01:17:03.994 --> 01:17:07.371
Power bomb,
compliments of Captain Insano.

1043
01:17:14.212 --> 01:17:17.298
All right, field goal.
Field goal. Go.

1044
01:17:17.382 --> 01:17:20.593
- Derek. Derek!
- Yeah.

1045
01:17:20.677 --> 01:17:23.804
Visualize the attack.
Go kick the ball. Kick it.

1046
01:17:23.889 --> 01:17:25.723
Hut!

1047
01:17:26.892 --> 01:17:29.435
How you doin', boy?

1048
01:17:29.519 --> 01:17:31.062
No, no, no!

1049
01:17:56.254 --> 01:17:58.589
What the hell is that?

1050
01:18:04.596 --> 01:18:07.807
What the hell is he up to?
That ain't in here!

1051
01:18:10.227 --> 01:18:14.772
Down by ten late in the fourth quarter,
Coach Klein opts for the field goal.

1052
01:18:14.856 --> 01:18:18.567
They have to hope for the onside kick
and a touchdown to tie the game.

1053
01:18:18.652 --> 01:18:22.988
Dan, look what we have here.
Boucher's in the game as a blocker.

1054
01:18:23.073 --> 01:18:26.450
Last game of the year.
Can't hold anything back now.

1055
01:18:28.036 --> 01:18:29.328
Set!

1056
01:18:33.458 --> 01:18:35.501
The snap. It's a fake!

1057
01:18:39.047 --> 01:18:42.967
Boucher's out in front!
A great block!

1058
01:18:43.051 --> 01:18:47.138
And a second one!
Touchdown, Mud Dogs!

1059
01:18:47.222 --> 01:18:50.349
Boucher led him all the way!

1060
01:18:53.937 --> 01:18:56.230
Red Beaulieu is steaming, Dan.

1061
01:18:56.314 --> 01:18:58.899
He sees his perfect season
slipping away.

1062
01:18:58.984 --> 01:19:02.778
The Cougars' lead is down to three.

1063
01:19:07.284 --> 01:19:10.578
Mud Dogs need the ball if they're
gonna have a shot at overtime.

1064
01:19:10.662 --> 01:19:14.165
And Bobby Boucher
is now on the kickoff team.

1065
01:19:14.249 --> 01:19:17.001
Last game of the year.
Can't hold anything back.

1066
01:19:17.085 --> 01:19:18.085
I know.

1067
01:19:20.088 --> 01:19:21.505
Who's it gonna be?

1068
01:19:21.590 --> 01:19:25.342
Who's it gonna be?
Who's it gonna be?

1069
01:19:28.513 --> 01:19:31.599
Oh, yeah. There's my bitch.

1070
01:19:31.683 --> 01:19:33.851
The ball must travel ten yards.

1071
01:19:36.688 --> 01:19:38.773
It's loose!

1072
01:19:38.857 --> 01:19:41.942
- Mud Dogs football! Mud Dogs football!
- All right!

1073
01:19:42.027 --> 01:19:45.112
- Mama, I got the football! I got it...
- What a vicious hit!

1074
01:19:45.197 --> 01:19:46.947
That was a cheap shot.

1075
01:19:50.076 --> 01:19:54.789
What a dumb penalty. That puts the Mud
Dogs in field goal range for the tie.

1076
01:19:54.873 --> 01:19:58.459
- I'm not sure Boucher can get up.
- Oh, my baby!

1077
01:20:05.008 --> 01:20:06.717
It's still cold.

1078
01:20:08.428 --> 01:20:10.513
Excuse me. Out of my way.

1079
01:20:13.391 --> 01:20:16.227
Dan, you hate to see this happen.

1080
01:20:25.570 --> 01:20:28.155
Now that's high quality H20.

1081
01:20:29.407 --> 01:20:32.243
You go on, now!
Make it happen, Bobby!

1082
01:20:36.248 --> 01:20:38.499
The Waterboy just needed some water.

1083
01:20:38.583 --> 01:20:41.752
Wow, Dan. You think that up
all by yourself?

1084
01:20:41.837 --> 01:20:43.212
Shut up, Brent.

1085
01:20:47.425 --> 01:20:49.844
- You OK?
- He tried to open a can ofwhoop-ass.

1086
01:20:49.928 --> 01:20:53.055
- I wouldn't let him.
- I have an idea for the last play.

1087
01:20:53.139 --> 01:20:56.892
You haven't done this before.
The offense is gonna line up like this.

1088
01:20:56.977 --> 01:21:00.604
- You're gonna be right here.
- There'll be no tie here today.

1089
01:21:00.689 --> 01:21:04.358
Coach Klein is sending
his offense back onto the field.

1090
01:21:04.442 --> 01:21:08.779
- He's going for the win right now.
- This is a real gutsy call, Brent.

1091
01:21:08.864 --> 01:21:11.615
He'll either be a hero
or a goat because of this.

1092
01:21:11.700 --> 01:21:15.119
And Dan,
Bobby Boucher is back on the field.

1093
01:21:15.203 --> 01:21:19.373
He is now playing offense!
We know. We know.

1094
01:21:19.457 --> 01:21:22.626
Meaney, if they give
that Waterboy the football,

1095
01:21:22.711 --> 01:21:27.047
I don't care if you have to stab him!
Do not let him get away. Understand?

1096
01:21:27.132 --> 01:21:31.051
- Yes, sir. Yes, sir!
- Do you understand me? Get in there!

1097
01:21:31.136 --> 01:21:32.595
Break!

1098
01:21:41.313 --> 01:21:43.814
- I'm ready, friend.
- Let's do it, Bobby.

1099
01:21:46.318 --> 01:21:47.902
Set! Set!

1100
01:21:47.986 --> 01:21:51.488
Forty-three! Red 43!
Hut, hut!

1101
01:23:08.733 --> 01:23:11.735
Touchdown! They won it!
The Mud Dogs win it!

1102
01:23:11.820 --> 01:23:16.115
Bobby Boucher's the hero!
He's gone from waterboy to savior!

1103
01:23:16.199 --> 01:23:18.325
Because he didn't
hold anything back!

1104
01:23:18.410 --> 01:23:23.122
Swannie's down on the field
with our hero, so let's go to Lynn now!

1105
01:23:25.333 --> 01:23:28.377
We did it! I can't believe it!
I can't believe it!

1106
01:23:28.461 --> 01:23:32.006
- Vicki, I love you!
- I love you, too, baby.

1107
01:23:32.090 --> 01:23:33.924
We're the champions!

1108
01:23:35.927 --> 01:23:39.847
Mr. Coach Klein, you got your manhood!
You got your manhood!

1109
01:23:39.931 --> 01:23:43.642
Bobby, congratulations.
You're the MVP of the Bourbon Bowl.

1110
01:23:43.727 --> 01:23:47.396
- How do you feel?
- I love Mama!

1111
01:24:07.375 --> 01:24:09.793
- Way to go, Bobby.
- Lookin' sharp, Bobby.

1112
01:24:09.878 --> 01:24:11.462
You the man, Bobby!

1113
01:24:11.546 --> 01:24:14.548
Bobby, I've been dreading
this day for a long time.

1114
01:24:14.632 --> 01:24:18.052
- But you got yourself a fine woman.
- Thank you, Mama.

1115
01:24:18.136 --> 01:24:21.096
Good luck, son.

1116
01:24:21.181 --> 01:24:23.140
This is the best day of my life!

1117
01:24:24.559 --> 01:24:28.729
- You just wait till tonight.
- What's gonna happen tonight?

1118
01:24:28.813 --> 01:24:31.065
- You'll see.
- You can do it!

1119
01:24:31.149 --> 01:24:35.027
You can do it all night long!

1120
01:24:40.116 --> 01:24:41.366
I'm gonna go do it!

1121
01:24:47.832 --> 01:24:49.750
Bobby, it's me!

1122
01:24:49.834 --> 01:24:52.878
- Your daddy, Roberto.
- Daddy?

1123
01:24:52.962 --> 01:24:56.256
I've seen you on the ESPN
when they was talkin' about

1124
01:24:56.341 --> 01:24:59.551
- you being drafted by the NFL.
- Not going to the NFL.

1125
01:24:59.636 --> 01:25:02.221
I'm gonna stay in school and graduate.

1126
01:25:02.305 --> 01:25:06.183
The hell with school, dopey! Take the
money! You and me could be partners,

1127
01:25:06.267 --> 01:25:09.686
just like that Tiger Woods
and his daddy.

1128
01:25:18.446 --> 01:25:21.448
- Nice hit, Mama.
- Thanks, baby.

1129
01:25:21.533 --> 01:25:23.992
Now you go on and have some fun
becoming a man.

1130
01:25:29.000 --> 01:25:35.000
<font color="#00ffff">--Thank for Watching--</font>
[Encode, Sync or Sub by AreLift]
